          "kind": "text",
          "value": "A class of 352 students are arranged in rows such that the number of students in each row is 6 less than twice the number of rows. Find the number of rows."
        }
      ],
      "numerical_answer": 16,
      "numerical_tolerance": 0.01,
      "marks": 1,
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "explanation": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "value": "$r(2r - 6) = 352 \\implies 2r^2 - 6r - 352 = 0 \\implies r^2 - 3r - 176 = 0 \\implies (r - 16)(r + 11) = 0 \\implies r = 16$."
        }
